Yendory Engine — origin of the code

crates/yendory-engine/src/model/{mod.rs,tape.rs,cache.rs,golden.rs} and
crates/yendory-engine/src/tokenizer.rs are carried over from Neural Nova:

  repository: https://github.com/SirSkirt/novaai
  branch:     experimental/neural-nova
  commit:     1f456b5cb4b8f6c8ccdd91ad035387eb42ccbb3d (2026-10-15)
  paths:      neural-nova/src/nova2/*, neural-nova/src/tokenizer.rs
  license:    MIT (declared in neural-nova/Cargo.toml)

Changes made in Yendory: the type Nova2 is renamed Bicameral and the module nova2 is renamed
model; checkpoint I/O moved to model/checkpoint.rs (same .nnova2 layout, now byte-identical on
load -> save, and malformed files return errors instead of panicking); the KV cache re-windows
past max_tokens exactly like the reference; an id-level generate_cached_ids was added; code was
reformatted with rustfmt. The network mathematics and parameter layout are unchanged.

reference/ is the numpy specification written by Claude for the Nova-2 "Bicameral" design
(Nova2-Bicameral-architecture package and the step-19,000 training package, 2026-10-15).
docs/ARCHITECTURE.md and docs/EXPERIMENTS.md come from the same architecture package.

The name "Yendory" began as a word made up by an early version of Nova while she was learning
to communicate; her school was jokingly called "Yendory University".

The license for Yendory as a whole has not been chosen yet.
